    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/9/79438.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's been a difficult job to maintain deliberation and to talk on the floor and debate and do the kinds of things that historically I've written about in the book that always occurred. The great debates, the great challenges with one another on the floor, of the Senate to where today it's speeches and calling for votes. Trying to work together is the solution and it was a secret that is so well known that people who come to the Senate to work across the aisle and to support the president when they can and they don't when they won't count. And as I said, I'll support the president, whoever the president is. when I can, I won't, when I shouldn't. But I'll look for solutions. I'm not there to obstruct. It's the obstructionism and hyper-partisanship that we're seeing today that is really threatening the future of the Senate.",
