  {
    "episode_id": 79438,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/9/79438.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 17,
    "turn_text": "have. In other words, when you get elected, you're not just elected to represent the people that voted for you. You're elected to represent all the people, whether it's in the Senate whether it's president or governor or any other position. You reach out and you bring on more people who are supportive and you work for the good of everybody that you possibly can. The other math moving away from addition and multiplication is the vision and subtraction. You develop a base and you keep it very, very tight by appealing basically only to that base. And the rest of the world, it really doesn't matter. It's only your base. And you can win elections that way from time to time, but you can't lead. You can't govern. You can't be inability to get things done for everyone if you're focused just on a base. President Trump has a base. He focuses on his base, and unfortunately, the other elected leaders who share that base, and that's all they play to.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "When elected, a leader represents all people, not just those who voted for them.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Leaders should reach out to and include supporters beyond their immediate base.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The goal of leadership is to work for the good of everyone possible.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Focusing solely on a political base leads to exclusion of broader constituencies.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "A strategy based on maintaining a narrow base through selective appeal is unsustainable for governance.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "President Trump focuses primarily on his political base.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      },
      {
        "text": "Other elected leaders who align with Trump’s base focus exclusively on that group.",
        "confidence": 0.84
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Effective leadership requires inclusive representation and broad-based support.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "True governance depends on cooperation across diverse groups rather than polarization.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Political success measured by election wins does not equate to effective leadership.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The legitimacy of public office rests on serving all constituents, not just partisans.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Polarizing strategies may secure short-term electoral gains but undermine long-term policy effectiveness.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a moral obligation for elected officials to prioritize collective well-being over partisan loyalty.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      },
      {
        "text": "Leaders who ignore non-base populations cannot build consensus or pass meaningful legislation.",
